{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #416: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $V(x)$ count the number of $n\\leq x$ such that $\\phi(m)=n$ is solvable. Does $V(2x)/V(x)\\to 2$? Is there an asymptotic formula for $V(x)$? Current best: Unfortunately this falls just short of an asymptotic formula for $V(x)$ and determining whether $V(2x)/V(x)\\to 2$. In \\cite{Er79e} Erd\\H{o}s asks further to estimate the number of $n\\leq x$ such that the smallest solution to $\\phi(m)=n$ satisfies $kx<m\\leq (k+1)x$. Prize: no. OEIS: A264810. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_9840d44064577eae149c415818369bf768b7f47047be3a51581076a476b94dd7","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:416","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_1c09126a019c0895","object_root":"sha256:cf80e329140dc8c42e38393292dba7683756677c166111c3504a510f7609a527","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:416"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-